2. How long does a cheap ceramic coating last? Most cheap ceramic coatings last two to six months, depending on the product and how the car is washed and stored. DIY spray coatings tend to wear off faster than budget shop-applied packages, which use slightly stronger formulas.
3. What is the average ceramic coating cost? Ceramic coating costs range from around $20 for a DIY spray bottle to $1,500 or more for a full professional package with paint correction. The price reflects product grade, application process, and how long the protection is expected to last.
